# MagicSquare Project Rules

## Project Context
- Project: MagicSquare
- Domain: 4x4 magic square generation and validation
- Language: Python 3.13.13
- Methodology: Dual-Track TDD with Clean Architecture (ECB)

## Before Coding
- Review related tests and confirm existing test intent.
- Verify the target ECB layer and dependency direction first.

## During Coding
- Keep ECB boundaries intact; do not add cross-layer violations.
- Always include type hints for function parameters and return values.
- Follow TDD flow strictly: RED -> GREEN -> REFACTOR.

## After Coding
- Run pytest for impacted areas and check regressions.
- Warn if TDD violations are detected (no RED, weakened tests).
- Keep minimum test coverage at or above 80%.
